-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2.0.4 (2026-10-30)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Made the Ed521 provider's system-config call Debian's /usr/bin/openssl, so another OpenSSL first on PATH no longer hides the provider from status or refuses enable

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2.0.3 (2026-10-29)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Added openssl-provider-ed521: Ed521 verification configured in OpenSSL system-wide beside the default provider, so ICP-Brasil v7 validates out of the box
  * Made the Ed521 provider faster and stricter: projective arithmetic, cheap key decoding, the subgroup check at verification
  * Added tests against RFC 8032, ITI's v7 root and CRL, wrong domains, the truncated hash and malformed points, and proof that nothing else in OpenSSL changes
  * Made the Ed521 message on the certificates page accurate, closable and gone when nothing is missing, in nine languages
  * Added the missing cmake and ninja-build build dependencies

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2.0.2 (2026-10-19)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Ignored browser profiles without explicitly selected certificate groups
  * Kept locked selected profiles safely deferred in status and the journal without repeated desktop alerts
  * Preserved notifications for update failures, certificate changes and new choices

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2.0.1 (2026-10-14)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Removed the integration with KIO's certificate manager and the dependency on a patched KIO
  * Added import of the chosen chain into gpgsm for Kleopatra, with trust only when you confirm it
  * Added removal of what was imported and of the trust entries that 2.0.0 added without asking
  * Made gpgsm and Kleopatra optional, shown only where gpgsm exists

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 2.0.0 (2026-10-14)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Rebuilt on Qt 6 and KDE Frameworks 6 with a Kirigami application, a System Settings module and a KAuth helper
  * Kept the sparky-ca command, the numbered text menu and the desktop entry name
  * Added a verified catalogue of ICP-Brasil certificates with pinned roots, ITI hashes and signed CRLs
  * Added installation in the system, Waterfox, Firefox and Chromium
  * Added A1 import, A3 token registration and optional KDE Wallet storage of passwords
  * Added a daily timer that keeps the chosen groups current and can be turned off
  * Added complete Brazilian Portuguese and Polish translations

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2018-03-29)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Changed sparky-xterm settings

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2018-02-19)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Added remsu to execute in desktop file

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2018-02-18)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Initial release
